1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
Buying ONE new tire for an
all-wheel-drive car?

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
Worth checking the other three first.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,400
AWD needs all four tires turning
at nearly the same rate

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,000
Deeper tread = a slightly bigger tire

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,200
One taller tire turns slower
than the other three

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,000
That difference can strain
the drivetrain

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,200
Your owner's manual lists a max
tread-depth difference

8
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:25,000
One clue: measure all four,
not just the flat one

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:27,400
Don't guess.

10
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:30,000
Nick's Tire & Auto · Euclid Ave,
Cleveland
